# Flow repository instructions for Cursor

Read `AGENTS.md` before editing. It is the canonical short agent contract.
Read `docs/project/agentic-loop.md` for dispatch, claiming, deduplication,
verification, review, and backpressure. Read
`docs/project/repository-structure.md` before adding or moving files.

Do not treat this file as a project-status snapshot. Current priorities come
from `ROADMAP.md` and GitHub. Current health comes from CI. Current language
behaviour comes from tests, `docs/LANGUAGE_SPEC.md`, and working examples.

The repository has two compiler hosts: the self-hosted compiler under
`compiler/` and the full/reference Python-host compiler under `src/flow/`.
The public command surface is `./flow`. Follow the bootstrap rules in
`AGENTS.md` for changes under `compiler/src/`.

Never create duplicate implementations because two directory layouts both look
plausible. `tools/` is the canonical home for long-lived developer tools;
`scripts/` should contain thin automation or shims.

Before implementation, search open pull requests for overlap. Prefer completing
or reviewing existing work over creating another branch. For a scoped change,
run the narrow proof that exercises it and the repository gate appropriate to
the touched surface. Record the evidence in the pull request.
